# SEO / AEO page rules

Research **before** writing any new tool, guide, hub, or example page. Follow `docs/SEO-GUARDRAILS.md` and the checklist below (from the site page-checklist).

## Before you write
- One primary query; name the intent (do / know / compare / navigate).
- Check top 5 SERP formats and avoid cannibalizing an existing URL.
- List 3–6 secondary questions → H2s and FAQ.

## Structure
- One H1 matching the query.
- Answer first: 40–60 words with a number or verdict; on tools the calculator sits above the fold on mobile (≤450px to first input).
- Guides: `answerFirst` + `takeaways` (3–5 bullets) before byline/body.
- Hubs/home: lead + first tool card above the fold (no disclaimer/ad before the card grid).
- Worked example with real numbers; at least one table you made.
- Visible Published / Last updated matching schema and sitemap lastmod.

## Metadata
- Title 30–60 chars (final with brand ≤65), unique; primary query near the start.
- Meta description 70–155 chars, unique, answer/benefit first.
- Absolute https canonical via `BaseLayout` + `siteConfig.siteUrl` only.
- Robots: index,follow for real pages; noindex for embeds.
- OG/Twitter + 1200×630 PNG og:image; `lang` + viewport set.

## Schema
- Valid JSON-LD; BreadcrumbList except homepage.
- Tools: WebApplication (offers price 0, OS Any); Guides: Article; FAQPage only when FAQ is visible.

## Trust
- Every rate/formula cites a primary source; reuse `src/data/fees.ts` — never invent rates.
- Byline links to About; financial disclaimer on tools (not as an FAQ item).

## Ship
- Page in sitemap; `npm run build && npm test && npm run audit` (includes `audit:pages`).
- Spot-check mobile 390×844: no overflow, tap targets ≥44px, cookie bar ≤56px.
